  text: At PrizePicks, we are the fastest-growing sports company in North America, as recognized by Inc. 5000. As the leading platform for Daily Fan
  text: We’re looking for a relationship-driven, detail-oriented Trading Card Buyer to source inventory, build a strong buying network, and own the 
  text: This is a hands-on buying role—not just an administrative position. You’ll represent the business at card shows, develop relationships with 
  text: The ideal candidate is comfortable making deals face-to-face and equally committed to keeping accurate records behind the scenes.
# What you’ll do:
# Buying & Relationship Development
  text: Travel to card shows and buying events to source inventory and establish new relationships.
  text: Build and maintain a network of collectors, dealers, and other inventory sources.
  text: Develop repeat buying opportunities through consistent outreach, follow-up, and reliable deal execution.
  text: Negotiate purchases within approved budgets and buying parameters, seeking approval for exceptions.
  text: Track buying opportunities and share market observations that inform purchasing decisions.
# Deal Execution & Payments
  text: Document each purchase, including the seller, cards acquired, agreed pricing, payment terms, and delivery arrangements.
  text: Coordinate timely payments to sellers and customers for completed, approved deals using Ramp and other approved payment methods.
  text: Verify payment information and supporting documentation before submitting or releasing payments.
  text: Track open invoices, outstanding payments, and unresolved deal items through completion.
  text: Communicate clearly with sellers about payment status, shipping, and any discrepancies.
# Inventory & Financial Accountability
  text: Own the workflow from purchase through inventory intake, ensuring every acquired item has an accurate digital record.
  text: Maintain inventory details such as player, year, set, card number, variation, grade, certification number where applicable, purchase cost, a
  text: Record item-level costs for individual cards and allocate costs across bulk purchases using an agreed methodology.
